---
import Definition from '../../../layouts/Definition.astro';
import Mermaid from '../../../components/Mermaid.astro';
import StagePreview from '../../../components/screens/StagePreview';
---

<Definition title="Guild Counter" section="Journey">
  <StagePreview
    client:only="react"
    slot="preview"
    glb="assets/stages/city_e/s00e_sa2/lndmd/s00e_sa2_m.glb"
    spawn={[0.06, 2, 12.95]}
    cameraOffset={[0, 10, 16]}
  />

  <h2>Context</h2>
  <p>Quest management hub. Accept missions, report completions, cancel active quests. Also has the storage counter.</p>

  <h2>Lighting</h2>
  <p>
    The mood rig is data-authored (#656): <code>data/stage_configs/city-lights/s00e_sa2.json</code>
    holds the omni lights (positions, color, energy, range, attenuation, shadows) and the ambient
    override in Godot units. It is authored in the web <code>#/city-lab</code> tool, which previews
    the values 1:1 against the scene, and loaded by
    <code>CityAreaBase._add_authored_lights</code> at scene entry. Until a sidecar lands, the
    legacy rig (seven warm omnis strung down the hallway at <code>y=4</code>, well above the
    −10.67 floor) still rides.
  </p>

  <h2>NPCs</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Guild Counter NPC</strong> — accept/report/cancel quests</li>
    <li><strong>Storage NPC</strong> — deposit/withdraw items</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Exits</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>South → <a href="/journey/city/market">Market</a></li>
    <li>East → <a href="/journey/city/teleport">Teleport</a></li>
    <li>West → <a href="/journey/city/office">Principal's Office</a></li>
  </ul>

  <Mermaid chart={`flowchart LR
    A[Office] --- B[Guild Counter]
    B --- C[Market]
    B --- D[Teleport]
  `} />
</Definition>
